[28.684168, "o", "# pysed\r\n\r\nA pure-Python replacement for GNU sed 4.9, for the minimal images that ship\r\nwithout sed.\r\n\r\n- `pysed/sed.py` — the command (`python3 /app/pysed/sed.py ...`)\r\n- `docs/sed.txt` — the GNU sed manual\r\n"]
